cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Smart Stop: an all-way stop sign plus a camera and a green flash for each approach. A simulation study"
version: "0.1"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24602948
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Tyler
    given-names: Patrick
repository-code: "https://github.com/tyresius/smart-stop"
abstract: >-
  A simulation study of an all-way stop sign with a camera and a green flash
  for each approach, which releases non-conflicting cars together and lets a
  car flashed at the line roll through. Two designs are compared, one that
  reads turn signals and one that ignores them, against a modelled all-way
  stop, a mini-roundabout and an actuated signal on an isolated single-lane
  four-way intersection. Includes the technical report, code, result files,
  tests and the audit record. All results are simulated and relative to
  modelled alternatives, not field measurements.
keywords:
  - traffic simulation
  - intersection control
  - all-way stop
  - traffic engineering
